            <ArticleTitle>[Future-oriented design of ambulatory surgery. Organizational aspects and medical options].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>986-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00101-011-1959-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ambulatory surgery continues to grow and is slowly becoming routine in the majority of cases. Although the development of ambulatory surgery in Germany appears to be somewhat delayed, this is actually a chance to learn from worldwide experiences and avoid the mistakes others made earlier. This article investigates current trends and developments in day case surgery and discusses the extended role and influence of the anesthetist in the perioperative setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
